# GPAC core API functions actually imported (from "env") by the filters this
# minimal build is meant to be used with (image/audio decode+transcode via
# writegen - see test-player/*.js's "solver_minimal_1" usages). Generated by
# disassembling each filter's *_1.wasm (wasm-dis) and collecting its "env"
# gf_* imports; symbols only needed by filters that require full gpac (isom/
# scenegraph/compositor, e.g. isobmff, theora, libmpeg2's mp4 muxing path -
# those explicitly use "solver_1", never "solver_minimal_1") are excluded on
# purpose, since gpac_minimal doesn't build ISOBMFF/scenegraph/compositor
# support at all. If a new filter needs to be paired with solver_minimal and
# fails to dlopen with an "undefined symbol" error, re-run the same
# wasm-dis scan against that filter's wasm and add whatever's missing here
# (as long as it's actually defined in libgpac_static.a - GPAC_DISABLE_ISOM
# and friends mean plenty of gf_isom_*/gf_sc_*/gf_scene_*/gf_bifs_* symbols
